276
00:14:33.990 --> 00:14:37.030
<v Wes Hart>She'd stopped asking. That's
when I should have been scared.

277
00:14:37.070 --> 00:14:39.612
<v Wes Hart>Not when she was asking. When she stopped.

278
00:14:41.262 --> 00:14:42.832
<v Jonathon>What made you go to the table?

279
00:14:43.170 --> 00:14:46.870
<v Wes Hart>Honestly? Nothing heroic.
My daughter was about nine.

280
00:14:46.970 --> 00:14:50.500
<v Wes Hart>And she brought her plate over to the
recliner and sat on the floor next to it.

281
00:14:50.510 --> 00:14:52.372
<v Wes Hart>Because that's where her dad was.

282
00:14:52.785 --> 00:14:53.645
<v Jonathon>Oh, man.

283
00:14:54.090 --> 00:14:57.540
<v Wes Hart>Yeah. She wasn't making a point.
She just wanted to eat with her dad.

284
00:14:57.550 --> 00:15:01.540
<v Wes Hart>And I looked down at her on the floor,
eating off her lap, and I thought, what am I

285
00:15:01.550 --> 00:15:03.790
<v Wes Hart>doing? What am I waiting on?

286
00:15:03.970 --> 00:15:06.330
<v Wes Hart>Which is funny, because
that's the question Mr.

287
00:15:06.430 --> 00:15:09.950
<v Wes Hart>Abernathy asked me about a year
