291
00:15:20.590 --> 00:15:22.375
<v Wes Hart>gets read at every wedding.

292
00:15:22.743 --> 00:15:23.370
<v Jonathon>Ours.

293
00:15:23.752 --> 00:15:24.690
<v Wes Hart>Everybody's.

294
00:15:24.890 --> 00:15:27.210
<v Wes Hart>And in the middle of it, Paul says this.

295
00:15:27.550 --> 00:15:32.720
<v Wes Hart>"When I was a child, I talked like a child,
I thought like a child, I reasoned like

296
00:15:32.730 --> 00:15:33.530
<v Wes Hart>a child.

297
00:15:33.630 --> 00:15:37.870
<v Wes Hart>When I became a man, I put the
ways of childhood behind me."

298
00:15:38.113 --> 00:15:40.450
<v Wes Hart>And here's the context in two sentences.

299
00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:44.110
<v Wes Hart>Paul's writing to a church in
Corinth that had everything.

300
00:15:44.230 --> 00:15:46.660
<v Wes Hart>Gifts, talent, big moments.

301
00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:51.920
<v Wes Hart>And they were acting like kids with it,
everybody chasing the impressive stuff and

302
00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:54.950
<v Wes Hart>nobody loving anybody on a regular day.

303
00:15:55.142 --> 00:15:57.650
<v Jonathon>So, a church full of guys like me.

304
00:15:57.946 --> 00:16:01.670
<v Wes Hart>A church full of highlight
reels. And look at the verb.

305
00:16:02.010 --> 00:16:07.410
<v Wes Hart>"I put the ways of childhood behind
me." He did it. It's not a birthday.

306
00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:12.138
<v Wes Hart>You don't turn thirty and wake up
