307
00:16:12.510 --> 00:16:13.546
<v Jonathon>What's the something?

308
00:16:13.930 --> 00:16:17.090
<v Wes Hart>For me, it was the
recliner. That's not a joke.

309
00:16:17.550 --> 00:16:21.030
<v Wes Hart>The recliner was where I went
to be a kid on a Tuesday.

310
00:16:21.530 --> 00:16:26.750
<v Wes Hart>Nobody needs anything from me, the TV's
talking, I don't have to be present.

311
00:16:27.190 --> 00:16:31.530
<v Wes Hart>That was childhood. That was
me reasoning like a child.

312
00:16:31.846 --> 00:16:34.170
<v Jonathon>And for me it was 1604.

313
00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:36.716
<v Wes Hart>For you it was 1604.

314
00:16:37.149 --> 00:16:42.480
<v Wes Hart>And then Jesus says something in Luke sixteen
that I think is the whole Tuesday idea

315
00:16:42.490 --> 00:16:43.870
<v Wes Hart>in one sentence.

316
00:16:43.990 --> 00:16:48.850
<v Wes Hart>He's telling a story about a manager
